  "id": "DrugBank_DB00876 - MONDO_grouped_1200_1134_15512_5080_100078",
  "verbalization": "Eprosartan is associated with Hypertension through a series of indirect pathways, all of which involve the treatment of Hypertensive Disorder. The evidence suggests that Eprosartan may be repurposed for hypertension due to its ability to influence the treatment of Hypertensive Disorder, which in turn is linked to hypertension. This relationship is supported by the shared indication of Hypertensive Disorder across multiple pathways, indicating a potential overlap in therapeutic mechanisms. The presence of multiple pathways pointing to Hypertensive Disorder as a common intermediate suggests that Eprosartan may exert its effects through a mechanism that modulates physiological processes related to blood pressure regulation. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Eprosartan to be used in the management of hypertension, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
